title The loop that waited on itself
prompt Two shells are still running -- work until all shells complete, then report.
think KEATON CAUGHT A FAULT NO GUARD AND NO TIMEOUT WOULD HAVE. Two background shells I armed read until not pgrep -f process_fanout_scan.sh --sample, then slept and asked again. The pattern sits in the waiting shell's own command line, so pgrep matched the loop itself every pass. The census they waited for had finished long before; both ran on.
think THIS IS %541, %569 AND %587 IN A SPELLING NONE OF THEM NAMED, and the failure mode inverts. Those had a command-line pattern reach a PEER and kill it, which is loud. A self-match that WAITS is silent: a loop waiting on itself reads exactly like a loop waiting on real work, and its task file at zero bytes reads exactly like a job still working.
think THE BOUNDED TOOL WAS RIGHT THE WHOLE TIME. Asked the same question, tools/f/fleet_call.sh --pattern answers would_send=0, refused_self=1, refused_prose=1 -- it resolves each candidate's working directory and declines the caller and a prompt that merely contains the words. The tree built the cure for the kill face of this wound and it covers the wait face unchanged.
obs I HAD READ THE CLAUSE ALOUD IN THIS SAME SESSION. The baton names the deed as resolving a pid from a command-line pattern BY ANY TOOL, and lists pkill, pgrep, ps piped to grep, and a proc walk. I typed it anyway, because the idiom arrived as a WAIT rather than as a kill -- and because the harness's own guidance offers this exact until form for waiting on background work. The wound lives at the seam between a host idiom and this tree's law, which is a place no guard here can read.
obs THE WATCHER'S OWN SLEEP WAS IDENTIFIED AND LEFT ALONE. One of the four sleeping processes was a child of fleet_watch.sh at pid 14993, cwd this tree. Resolving parents through /proc/PID/status before touching anything is what kept a fleet mechanism running while two of my own shells came down.
obs THE STOP WAS MADE THROUGH THE HARNESS'S OWN TASK CONTROL rather than by signal, so no pid was resolved from a pattern to end the fault that came from resolving a pid from a pattern.
